7. INDEPENDENT IMPLEMENTATION OF THE TWEAKER
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Tweaker's PServer client, fan controller, tuning planner and family catalog are independent
implementations. PULSE (https://github.com/keiretrogaming/pulse) and ClusterTune
(https://github.com/AurelioB/ClusterTune) are references for published hardware facts, not bundled
source code. The CPU frequencies credited to ClusterTune are device-reported hardware values.

Credits for ideas and techniques, which are not license statements:
  - ClusterTune by AurelioB: https://github.com/AurelioB/ClusterTune
  - PULSE by keiretrogaming: https://github.com/keiretrogaming/pulse
  - O2P Tweaks by FeralAI: https://github.com/FeralAI/o2ptweaks.app

The Mimir app reaches the same vendor PServer service from `PServerHost.kt`. The technique
(getting the `PServerBinder` from `android.os.ServiceManager` by reflection and sending it a
transaction that carries a shell command) is documented by those three projects. `PServerHost.kt` and `MimirTuner.kt` are independent implementations of the interface facts: a service name, a transaction code, an argument shape, and the
sysfs paths the kernel publishes.

`mimir-tweaker/NOTICE.md` has the detailed credits for the Tweaker.


